    "summary": "On July 6, 2026, Singapore prosecutors handed Alan Wei Zhaolun, 50, nine additional charges – three counts of money laundering and six counts of fraud – bringing his total to 11, in a case the article describes as allegedly linked to chipmaker Nvidia. Police said the fraud charges allege that Wei conspired with Aaron Woon Guo Jie and Jenny Lim to commit fraud linked to purchases of servers from three suppliers – Dell, Super Micro Computer and Asus – by falsely representing to those suppliers that one of the Aperia Group companies would be the end-user of the servers. Three Aperia Group companies were also charged with fraud the same day: Aperia International (five counts), Aperia Cloud Services (II) (two counts) and A-Speed Infotech (one count). The item gives no volume of chips or servers, no Nvidia figures, and does not allege wrongdoing by Nvidia.",
